# .env -- host-local compose overrides for docker-compose.yml, NEVER
# committed (see .gitignore's ".env" entry).
#
# Copy this file to the repo root as `.env` and edit it:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# podman-compose / docker compose reads a repo-root .env automatically for
# `${VAR}` substitution in docker-compose.yml -- no wrapper script, no
# extra loader. Every value below is optional; leaving `.env` absent (or
# any single line unset) falls back to the default already baked into
# docker-compose.yml, so a fresh clone with no `.env` still brings the
# stack up.

# artifact-svc's tarball-extraction root for published artifact bytes.
# Nests under ARTIFACT_SVC_FEEDBACK_ROOT by default (see below), so it
# rarely needs setting on its own -- override ARTIFACT_SVC_FEEDBACK_ROOT
# instead to move both together. Set this independently only if you want
# staged bytes on a different disk than the feedback database; doing so
# needs its own volume line added to docker-compose.yml, since the
# default volume mount only follows ARTIFACT_SVC_FEEDBACK_ROOT.
# ARTIFACT_SVC_STAGE_ROOT=${HOME}/.local/share/artifacts/stage

# artifact-svc's durable root: feedback.db (sqlite) and uploaded review
# files. The default volume mount covers this path, so overriding it here
# also relocates where the container's data actually lands on the host.
# ARTIFACT_SVC_FEEDBACK_ROOT=${HOME}/.local/share/artifacts

# Extra Django ALLOWED_HOSTS entries for artifact-svc, comma-separated.
# Add a Tailscale MagicDNS hostname here to reach the service over
# `tailscale serve` without editing the tracked compose file.
# ARTIFACT_SVC_ALLOWED_HOSTS=127.0.0.1,localhost,your-host.your-tailnet.ts.net

# --- Not wired up yet: kb-svc's KB_HOME and bd-svc's BEADS_HUB_DIR -----
#
# docker-compose.yml still hardcodes these to ${HOME}/.knowledgebase and
# ${HOME}/.beads-hub (environment AND volumes both reference the literal
# path, not a variable), so setting KB_HOME or BEADS_HUB_DIR here does
# NOT relocate the containerized services -- only the bare-host CLI code
# paths that read those env vars directly. To actually move kb-svc's or
# bd-svc's data root, edit docker-compose.yml's environment and volumes
# lines for that service together (see
# docs/agent-workbench-hardening-plan.md, H3). Recommended follow-up if
# this ever becomes a real need: give them the same
# `${VAR:-${HOME}/...}` treatment as ARTIFACT_SVC_FEEDBACK_ROOT above, in
# both the environment and volumes lines together.
